perties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablecellspanning","children":[{"type":"text","value":"enableCellSpanning?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional enableCellSpanning: boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L87","children":[{"type":"text","value":"features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:87"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turns this column off for cell spanning even when the table allows it.\nDefaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"spancolumns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"spanColumns?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional spanColumns: number | (context) => number;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L102","children":[{"type":"text","value":"features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:102"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Makes this column's cell span the given number of columns per row,\nstarting at itself and counted in the order columns actually render."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" or less for no span. Larger values are clamped to the end of\nthe cell's pinned region, so a span can never cross the start-pinned,\ncenter, or end-pinned boundary; pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" for \"the rest of my\nregion\". Hidden columns are not counted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{ accessorKey: 'label', spanColumns: ({ row }) => row.original.isSummary ? Infinity : 1 }","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"spanrows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"spanRows?"}]},{"type":"code","value":"optional spanRows: boolean | (context) => boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L127","children":[{"type":"text","value":"features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:127"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merges adjacent rows in this column into a single vertically spanning\ncell."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" merges rows whose values for this column are the same value\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.is"},{"type":"text","value":"). Nullish values never merge under the default comparison."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A predicate replaces the comparison entirely and decides whether "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row"},{"type":"text","value":"\njoins the run anchored at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anchorRow"},{"type":"text","value":"; it may merge nullish values. It is\ncalled once per candidate row each time the span index rebuilds, and each\ncall allocates one context object, so keep it cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spans are always recomputed from the rows that are actually rendered, so\nsorting, filtering, and paging only change which rows are adjacent. Runs\nnever cross a page boundary, a pinned-row section boundary, a change of\nposition in the row tree, or a grouped row. Ignored while this column is\ngrouped."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{ accessorKey: 'department', spanRows: true }","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"interface-columndef-cellspanningtfeatures-tdata-tvalue","text":"Interface: ColumnDef_CellSpanning<TFeatures, TData, TValue>","level":1},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfeatures","text":"TFeatures","level":3},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"enablecellspanning","text":"enableCellSpanning?","level":3},{"id":"spancolumns","text":"spanColumns?","level":3},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"spanrows","text":"spanRows?","level":3},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Interface: ColumnDef\\_CellSpanning\\<TFeatures, TData, TValue\\>\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:78](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L78)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* [`TableFeatures`](TableFeatures.md)\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* [`RowData`](../type-aliases/RowData.md)\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue` *extends* [`CellData`](../type-aliases/CellData.md) = [`CellData`](../type-aliases/CellData.md)\n\n## Properties\n\n### enableCellSpanning?\n\n```ts\noptional enableCellSpanning: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:87](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L87)\n\nTurns this column off for cell spanning even when the table allows it.\nDefaults to `true`.\n\n***\n\n### spanColumns?\n\n```ts\noptional spanColumns: number | (context) => number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:102](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L102)\n\nMakes this column's cell span the given number of columns per row,\nstarting at itself and counted in the order columns actually render.\n\nReturn `1` or less for no span. Larger values are clamped to the end of\nthe cell's pinned region, so a span can never cross the start-pinned,\ncenter, or end-pinned boundary; pass `Infinity` for \"the rest of my\nregion\". Hidden columns are not counted.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n{ accessorKey: 'label', spanColumns: ({ row }) => row.original.isSummary ? Infinity : 1 }\n```\n\n***\n\n### spanRows?\n\n```ts\noptional spanRows: boolean | (context) => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:127](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L127)\n\nMerges adjacent rows in this column into a single vertically spanning\ncell.\n\n`true` merges rows whose values for this column are the same value\n(`Object.is`). Nullish values never merge under the default comparison.\n\nA predicate replaces the comparison entirely and decides whether `row`\njoins the run anchored at `anchorRow`; it may merge nullish values. It is\ncalled once per candidate row each time the span index rebuilds, and each\ncall allocates one context object, so keep it cheap.\n\nSpans are always recomputed from the rows that are actually rendered, so\nsorting, filtering, and paging only change which rows are adjacent. Runs\nnever cross a page boundary, a pinned-row section boundary, a change of\nposition in the row tree, or a grouped row. Ignored while this column is\ngrouped.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n{ accessorKey: 'department', spanRows: true }\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ColumnDef_CellSpanning\ntitle: ColumnDef_CellSpanning\n---\n\n# Interface: ColumnDef\\_CellSpanning\\<TFeatures, TData, TValue\\>\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:78](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L78)\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* [`TableFeatures`](TableFeatures.md)\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* [`RowData`](../type-aliases/RowData.md)\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue` *extends* [`CellData`](../type-aliases/CellData.md) = [`CellData`](../type-aliases/CellData.md)\n\n## Properties\n\n### enableCellSpanning?\n\n```ts\noptional enableCellSpanning: boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:87](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L87)\n\nTurns this column off for cell spanning even when the table allows it.\nDefaults to `true`.\n\n***\n\n### spanColumns?\n\n```ts\noptional spanColumns: number | (context) => number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:102](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L102)\n\nMakes this column's cell span the given number of columns per row,\nstarting at itself and counted in the order columns actually render.\n\nReturn `1` or less for no span. Larger values are clamped to the end of\nthe cell's pinned region, so a span can never cross the start-pinned,\ncenter, or end-pinned boundary; pass `Infinity` for \"the rest of my\nregion\". Hidden columns are not counted.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n{ accessorKey: 'label', spanColumns: ({ row }) => row.original.isSummary ? Infinity : 1 }\n```\n\n***\n\n### spanRows?\n\n```ts\noptional spanRows: boolean | (context) => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts:127](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/cell-spanning/cellSpanningFeature.types.ts#L127)\n\nMerges adjacent rows in this column into a single vertically spanning\ncell.\n\n`true` merges rows whose values for this column are the same value\n(`Object.is`). Nullish values never merge under the default comparison.\n\nA predicate replaces the comparison entirely and decides whether `row`\njoins the run anchored at `anchorRow`; it may merge nullish values. It is\ncalled once per candidate row each time the span index rebuilds, and each\ncall allocates one context object, so keep it cheap.\n\nSpans are always recomputed from the rows that are actually rendered, so\nsorting, filtering, and paging only change which rows are adjacent. Runs\nnever cross a page boundary, a pinned-row section boundary, a change of\nposition in the row tree, or a grouped row. Ignored while this column is\ngrouped.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\n{ accessorKey: 'department', spanRows: true }\n```\n"}
